{"Title":"An Act relative to the inventory tax","BillNumber":"S1806","DocketNumber":"SD1614","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"RCF0","Name":"Ryan C. Fattman","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/RCF0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-13T20:21:40.97"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"RCF0","Name":"Ryan C. Fattman","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/RCF0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-13T20:21:40.97"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S1806/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Mr. Fattman, a petition (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 1806) of Ryan C. Fattman for legislation relative to the inventory tax.  Revenue.","DocumentText":"\tSection 5 of chapter 59 of the General Laws, as appearing in the 2020 Official Edition, is hereby amended by inserting after clause Nineteenth the following clause:-\r\n\tNineteenth A. Merchandise situated in Massachusetts, including inventory held for sale; finished goods; products, goods, wares or stock in trade; work in progress; materials or supplies; and archived or stored goods.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J26","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J26"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}